{
  "summary": "Adds configuration and parameters for Testnet 5 (BIP 95), including chain parameters, DNS and fixed seeds, kernel C API support, and GUI/CLI integration. Testnet 5 eliminates the 20-minute minimum-difficulty exception from earlier testnets, sets a higher minimum difficulty (nBits 0x1a0fffff), and enforces BIP 54 (Consensus Cleanup) rules from block 1. Only the top seven commits belong to this PR, with the preceding commits implementing BIP 54 via stacked PR #35793.",
  "problem": "Testnet 3 and Testnet 4 frequently suffer from block storms and severe difficulty manipulation due to the 20-minute minimum-difficulty rule, disrupting developers and testers. Additionally, there is currently no public test network validating BIP 54 consensus cleanup rules from genesis.",
